This product includes map data and libraries from third parties, which remain
under their own licences. The two CC BY 4.0 sets below require attribution
wherever this work is redistributed; the rest are listed so that nobody has to
work out where a boundary came from.

  Natural Earth (https://www.naturalearthdata.com/) — country and region
  boundaries, lakes and shaded relief. Public domain.

  geoBoundaries (https://www.geoboundaries.org/) — detailed administrative
  boundaries, compositing national survey data. CC BY 4.0.

  GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org/) — town names, from cities1000, thinned.
  CC BY 4.0.

  OpenStreetMap contributors (https://www.openstreetmap.org/) — railways via
  OpenRailwayMap (https://openrailwaymap.app/), and waymarked trails and route
  lookup. ODbL.

  MapLibre GL JS (https://maplibre.org/) — vector map rendering. BSD 3-Clause.

  polygon-clipping (https://github.com/mfogel/polygon-clipping) — boolean
  operations on polygons. MIT.

Basemap tiles are served by CARTO (https://carto.com/basemaps/), OpenFreeMap
(https://openfreemap.org/), Esri World Imagery, and Mapbox
(https://www.mapbox.com/) under their own terms. The Mapbox basemap is drawn
only for a viewer who has supplied their own access token.
